returns exactly `0.0` forever, a C quirk I reproduced rather than \"fixed\"), all-ones, sign-bit-set, and mantissa-boundary values (`0xFFF`/`0x1000`).\n\n`cargo build --release` compiles clean with no warnings, and `c_src/` is untouched.\n\nTwo housekeeping notes for transparency:\n- A `rm -rf` cleanup of my scratch files was denied by the sandbox, so three throwaway artifacts remain in the tree: `build_c/` (the reference C build + diff harness) and `rust_syms.txt` files. They are inert and don't affect the crate, but you may want to delete them.\n- Early on, a couple of commands appeared to \"lose\" files: `$TMPDIR` writes didn't persist between calls, and one shell had retained `cd translation` as its working directory. Switching to absolute paths under the working tree resolved both — worth knowing if you see similar phantom failures."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1214,"cache_read_input_tokens":25018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1214,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08b5b5f1-fbe2-4eaa-94ba-92b26fb2feeb","uuid":"bd881e94-0943-4c00-a453-2ffbd7d2fcd5","timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:00:38.487Z"}
